WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:05.170
The infamous Star Wars bounty hunter Boba
Fett was supposed to be given his own movie

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:09.220
with a definitive backstory, but plans at
the studio suddenly changed.

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:10.220
Why?

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:13.700
Here's a look at the real reasons Disney won't
give Boba Fett his own film.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:18.900
It took three decades, but Han Solo finally
got proper revenge for the whole carbonite

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.180
thing by getting Boba Fett's solo movie cancelled.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:27.140
2018's Solo: A Star Wars Story wasn't exactly
a critical failure, but it was definitely

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:28.570
a commercial one.

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:33.110
Forbes called the Alden Ehrenreich-led spin-off
a "disaster from every point of view," and

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:34.120
they weren't kidding.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:40.480
Domestic receipts for Solo totaled just shy
of $214 million, which sounds like a lot until

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:45.989
you consider the fact that Disney reportedly
spent an estimated $400 million to make and

00:00:45.989 --> 00:00:47.130
promote the film.

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:50.530
That prompted Disney to look at the many reasons
Solo failed.

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:54.070
Much of it had to do with the film's well
publicized behind-the-scenes chaos, which

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:59.110
included Ehrenreich requiring acting lessons,
as well as the firing of directors Phil Lord

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:01.750
and Christopher Miller halfway through the
shoot.

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:06.110
But the biggest problem may have simply been
franchise fatigue, as Solo was the fourth

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:08.610
Star Wars movie in as many years.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:13.080
Disney CEO Bob Iger told The Hollywood Reporter
they just plain overdid it.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:17.380
"I think the mistake that I made, I take the
blame, was a little too much, too fast.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:21.100
You can expect some slowdown, but that doesn't
mean we're not going to make films."

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.900
But none of those films will be Boba Fett.

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:28.780
These days, films studios have to think globally,
as China has emerged as the largest film market

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:30.880
in the world behind the United States.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:36.670
But while some Disney-owned franchises, like
the Marvel Cinematic Universe, are huge overseas,

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:39.030
Star Wars has proven to be a tough sell in
China.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.180
How tough?

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:45.521
Solo made barely $10 million in China over
its opening weekend, while The Last Jedi was

00:01:45.521 --> 00:01:49.250
reportedly pulled early from Cinese theaters
for underperforming.

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:51.950
Rogue One star Donnie Yen told JoBlo,

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:57.229
"Chinese audiences didn't grow up with Star
Wars culture so unfortunately it didn't work.

00:01:57.229 --> 00:01:58.580
Marvel is a lot easier to understand.

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:01.520
Star Wars, there's a whole universe out there.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:06.060
Marvel, from the costumes, to the music, to
the idols, to the stars, it's much easier

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:08.940
to close the gap between the film itself and
the audience."

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:13.730
As Solo proved, without China as a financial
safety net, a Boba Fett movie is just too

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:14.780
risky to make.

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:20.960
When Disney purchased Lucasfilm in 2012, a
Boba Fett solo movie was one of the first

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:25.130
projects to be announced, with up-and-comer
Josh Trank attached to direct.

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:29.630
It was also one of the first projects to be
scrapped, after Trank drove Fox's Fantastic

00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:34.800
Four franchise into the ground in 2015 with
one of the biggest box office bombs of the

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:35.800
decade.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:40.650
But Disney didn't abandon the idea of a Boba
Fett film, as in early 2018, it was widely

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:45.440
reported that Logan director James Mangold
had been tapped to helm a revived Boba Fett

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:46.740
solo project.

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:51.580
But after Solo faceplanted, Mangold distanced
himself, calling all the Boba Fett rumors

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:52.709
"so much gossip."

00:02:52.709 --> 00:02:57.490
After being burned twice, it's no wonder Disney
decided not to start development for a third

00:02:57.490 --> 00:02:58.060
time.

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:02.940
The woman in charge of steering the Star Wars
universe for Disney is Kathleen Kennedy.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:08.010
A longtime friend and collaborator of George
Lucas, Kennedy signed a three-year contract

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:12.629
extension in September, 2018 to stay as the
president of Lucasfilm.

00:03:12.629 --> 00:03:17.280
And one of her first moves was to verify that
in the near term, Disney's focus is entirely

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:19.020
on completing Episode Nine.

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:22.840
In October, 2018, film journalist Eric Weber
tweeted,

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:27.460
"Kathleen Kennedy just confirmed to me Boba
Fett movie is 100 percent dead."

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:32.760
Much of the mystique of Boba Fett comes from
the combination of his iconically cool look

00:03:32.769 --> 00:03:34.620
and his mysterious backstory.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:38.980
Now that his story has been extensively told
in the prequel trilogy, though, much of that

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:43.430
mystique has faded, which may explain why
Disney is turning their attention to a different

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:46.350
Boba Fett related project: The Mandalorian.

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:51.720
Spearheaded by Iron Man director Jon Favreau,
The Mandalorian is a Star Wars TV series for

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:53.810
Disney's upcoming streaming service.

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:59.340
It focuses on a mysterious new figure wearing
the iconic Mandalorian armor made famous by

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:03.879
Boba Fett, allowing Disney to keep the cool
visuals while restoring some of the intrigue

00:04:03.879 --> 00:04:05.510
the prequels stripped away.

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:08.030
Favreau teased the show on Instagram, saying,

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:13.560
"After the stories of Jango and Boba Fett,
another warrior emerges in the Star Wars universe.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:18.019
The Mandalorian is set after the fall of the
Empire and before the emergence of the First

00:04:18.019 --> 00:04:19.019
Order.

00:04:19.019 --> 00:04:23.050
We follow the travails of a lone gunfighter
in the outer reaches of the galaxy far from

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:24.969
the authority of the New Republic."

00:04:24.969 --> 00:04:29.539
With The Mandalorian taking Boba Fett's place,
it looks like fans may have seen the last

00:04:29.539 --> 00:04:33.129
of the galaxy's most notorious bounty hunter,
for now, at least.

